Month = {SPR},
Abstract = {Public opinion regarding smoking and health has been of interest to
   polling companies since the 1940s. This article documents the rate of
   change in the public's awareness and beliefs about smoking and health in
   North America (the United States and Canada). It reports on four broad
   categories of opinions: public awareness of reports that smoking has
   been linked to lung cancer; beliefs that smoking is harmful to health
   and a cause of lung cancer; beliefs that smoking is a cause of diseases
   other than lung cancer; and beliefs about the health hazards of
   secondhand smoke.},
